<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12780" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-grĕdĭor</span></b> ,
			gressus, 3, v. dep.
		gradior, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to go down, march down, descend</i> (never, to go
			away, depart, like digredior— 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">freq. only after the Aug. period, esp. in Liv.
					and Tac.): de via in semitam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Cas. 3, 5, 40</span></i>
			 (dub.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">degressus ex arce,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 5,
					52</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">templo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 8,
					35</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">monte,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sall. J. 49, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">colle,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 50, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jugis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					1, 61</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Alpibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 66</span></i>
			
			<i>fin.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 67</span></i>
			 al.—<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">degrediente eo magnā prosequentium
					multitudine,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 13, 14</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">13, 54</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. H. 2, 51</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Agr.
			37</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 8, 16, 21, § 58</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in campum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 7,
					24</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">44, 5</span></i>
			<i>fin.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in specum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					2, 54 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in aequum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Agr.
					18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad pedes,</span>”
				<i>to alight, dismount</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 3,
					62 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">29, 2</span></i>. (In
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				de Or. 2, 19, 80</span></i>, the true reading is digredi.)</div>
